WEBVTT

00:00:00.158 --> 00:00:03.322
Likert-style responses illustrate ordinal data well.

00:00:03.322 --> 00:00:10.122
A five is higher than a four, but the psychological distance from one to two may not equal the distance from

00:00:10.122 --> 00:00:14.847
four to five. Means are commonly reported in practice, particularly for composite scales.

00:00:14.847 --> 00:00:17.582
But for a single coarse item, medians, distributions,

00:00:17.582 --> 00:00:22.242
and rank-based summaries may better respect the measurement assumptions.

00:00:22.242 --> 00:00:27.147
The important point is to recognize the assumption rather than use the mean automatically.

00:00:27.147 --> 00:00:32.477
Connect this idea to an e-commerce team preparing customer, purchase, and web-event data.

00:00:32.477 --> 00:00:37.617
Ask what could go wrong if the concept were misunderstood: could rows be duplicated,

00:00:37.617 --> 00:00:44.447
important records disappear, categories be interpreted incorrectly, or a report become difficult to reproduce?

00:00:44.447 --> 00:00:49.597
A strong analyst can explain both the SQL operation and the assumption behind it.

00:00:49.597 --> 00:00:54.480
After the example, summarize the idea in one plain-language sentence before moving on.
